nario_key":"vent_no_solutions","scenario":"They explicitly want to vent without receiving solutions.","required_evidence":"Direct rejection of advice or explicit request to vent, be heard, or unload.","disqualifiers":"Neutral frustration; safety crisis; viewer is the subject of the complaint and contact may escalate it.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"restrained","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"LISTEN FIRST, NO FIXES","template_card":{"label":"LISTEN FIRST","title":"Not a Fix-It Day","observation":"They have a lot to let out and have been clear that solutions would add pressure rather than help.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Try: “That sounds like a lot. I’m here for the unfiltered version.”"},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-002","family_key":"listening_and_venting","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"vent_needs_validation","scenario":"They want the difficulty acknowledged before any other response.","required_evidence":"Direct language about feeling dismissed, minimized, or wanting someone to understand.","disqualifiers":"No stated emotional impact; advice request; unsupported claim that others failed them.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"restrained","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"JUST HEAR THEM, VALIDATION FIRST","template_card":{"label":"VALIDATION FIRST","title":"Let the Hard Part Be Real","observation":"They are not asking for the situation to be made smaller. Being taken seriously would matter more than immediate reassurance.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Lead with: “It makes sense that this hurt.”"},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-003","family_key":"listening_and_venting","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"vent_about_unfair_treatment","scenario":"They describe unfair treatment and want room to process it.","required_evidence":"Direct account of feeling treated unfairly plus anger or desire to talk.","disqualifiers":"Unverified allegations presented as fact; legal details; advice to confront or retaliate.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"restrained","depth_level":"L5 Full","field_pattern":"Observation, distinct meaning, and one proportionate takeaway. Use only when each adds value.","label_options":"THE FULL RANT, HEAR THEM OUT","template_card":{"label":"HEAR THEM OUT","title":"They Need a Witness Before a Strategy","observation":"They are still processing an experience that felt unfair and are not ready to turn it into a problem-solving session.","meaning":"A small response fits better here than trying to solve the whole situation.","takeaway":"Offer a call where they can tell the story without being redirected."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-004","family_key":"listening_and_venting","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"vent_repeating_problem","scenario":"A recurring problem is wearing them down and they need patient listening.","required_evidence":"Explicit repetition plus frustration and an opening to talk.","disqualifiers":"One incident; generic advice; labeling them stuck or negative.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"restrained","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"SAME PROBLEM, LISTENING ROOM","template_card":{"label":"LISTENING ROOM","title":"The Repeat Is Part of the Weight","observation":"What is wearing them down is not only the latest incident, but having to face the same frustration again.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Ask whether they want to vent, then stay with this version of the story."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-005","family_key":"listening_and_venting","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"processing_big_decision_aloud","scenario":"They think best by talking through a decision without being told what to choose.","required_evidence":"Explicit desire to talk it out plus uncertainty and no request for a verdict.","disqualifiers":"Legal, medical, or financial decision; request for direct advice; viewer has a conflict of interest.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"restrained","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"TALK IT THROUGH, THINKING OUT LOUD","template_card":{"label":"THINKING OUT LOUD","title":"They Don’t Need a Verdict","observation":"They are trying to hear their own judgment more clearly, not hand the decision to someone else.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Offer to listen and reflect back what you hear, without choosing a side."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-006","family_key":"listening_and_venting","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"bad_day_low_words","scenario":"They had a hard day but have little energy to explain it fully.","required_evidence":"Direct statement of a hard day plus low capacity or difficulty finding words.","disqualifiers":"Silence alone; assuming a crisis; repeated pressure to disclose.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"restrained","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"LOW-WORD DAY, EASY OPENING","template_card":{"label":"LOW-WORD DAY","title":null,"observation":"They have had a difficult day and may not have enough energy to turn it into a full explanation yet.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Try: “You can give me the one-sentence version—or none at all.”"},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-007","family_key":"listening_and_venting","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"frustrated_wants_unfiltered_call","scenario":"They explicitly want a candid call or rant with the viewer.","required_evidence":"A direct invitation or stated desire to call and vent.","disqualifiers":"No invitation; viewer is unavailable; sensitive details the writer hid.","emotional_weight":"ordinary","tone_mode":"gentle_practical","depth_level":"L5 Full","field_pattern":"Observation, distinct meaning, and one proportionate takeaway. Use only when each adds value.","label_options":"OPEN LINE, RANT READY","template_card":{"label":"OPEN LINE","title":"The Unfiltered Version Is Waiting","observation":"They would rather talk naturally than package the experience into neat text updates.","meaning":"A small response fits better here than trying to solve the whole situation.","takeaway":"Offer a low-pressure call and let them choose when to start it."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-008","family_key":"listening_and_venting","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"disappointment_needs_room","scenario":"They are disappointed and want the loss acknowledged without forced positivity.","required_evidence":"Direct disappointment plus resistance to silver linings or premature reframing.","disqualifiers":"One minor inconvenience; making promises about future outcomes.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"restrained","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"NO SILVER LINING, LET IT LAND","template_card":{"label":"LET IT LAND","title":"The Bright Side Can Wait","observation":"They understand the future may hold other chances, but they need room for this disappointment to matter first.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Say: “I know you wanted this. I’m sorry it didn’t happen.”"},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-009","family_key":"listening_and_venting","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"grief_wants_memories","scenario":"They want to talk about someone or something they are grieving.","required_evidence":"Explicit grief plus invitation to remember, talk, or share stories.","disqualifiers":"Diagnosing grief; asking for private medical details; forcing conversation.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"restrained","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"MEMORY SPACE, STAY WITH IT","template_card":{"label":"MEMORY SPACE","title":"They Don’t Want the Story Changed","observation":"They want space to remember openly without the conversation being redirected away from grief.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Invite one memory and let them decide how long to stay there."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-010","family_key":"listening_and_venting","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"conflict_processing_before_response","scenario":"They need to process a conflict before deciding what to do.","required_evidence":"Direct statement that they are not ready to respond or choose a next step.","disqualifiers":"Encouraging avoidance indefinitely; taking sides; viewer is the conflict partner.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"restrained","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"PROCESSING FIRST, PAUSE BEFORE ACTION","template_card":{"label":"PROCESSING FIRST","title":"Clarity Hasn’t Arrived Yet","observation":"They are still sorting emotion from judgment and are not ready to turn the conflict into a decision.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Give them space to talk without pushing for a next move."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-011","family_key":"comfort_and_reassurance","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"lonely_wants_company","scenario":"They feel lonely and clearly want connection or company.","required_evidence":"Explicit loneliness plus desire for company, contact, or shared presence.","disqualifiers":"Being alone without distress; stated desire for space; assuming a call is welcome.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"gentle","depth_level":"L5 Full","field_pattern":"Observation, distinct meaning, and one proportionate takeaway. Use only when each adds value.","label_options":"A LITTLE CLOSER, COMPANY HELPS","template_card":{"label":"A LITTLE CLOSER","title":"Presence Matters More Than the Perfect Words","observation":"They are missing the feeling of having someone nearby, even without a serious conversation.","meaning":"A small response fits better here than trying to solve the whole situation.","takeaway":"Offer a quiet call or shared activity with no pressure to talk."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-012","family_key":"comfort_and_reassurance","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"homesick_wants_familiarity","scenario":"They are homesick and want something familiar.","required_evidence":"Explicit homesickness plus a known or stated familiar comfort.","disqualifiers":"Assuming they regret moving; exact location; proposing an expensive trip.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"gentle","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"FAMILIAR HELPS, CLOSE TO HOME","template_card":{"label":"FAMILIAR HELPS","title":"Bring a Little Home to Them","observation":"What they are missing is the ease of something familiar, not a major update or solution.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Send a voice note that feels ordinary, warm, and unmistakably you."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-013","family_key":"comfort_and_reassurance","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"anxious_before_event_wants_calm","scenario":"They feel nervous before an event and welcome calm reassurance.","required_evidence":"Explicit upcoming event, anxiety, and openness to reassurance or contact.","disqualifiers":"Medical panic; telling them there is nothing to worry about; event already used without distinct support evidence.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"gentle","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"STEADYING WORDS, BEFORE THE MOMENT","template_card":{"label":"STEADYING WORDS","title":"Keep the Reassurance Simple","observation":"They are nervous about what is ahead and have already named the kind of support that would feel useful.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Try: “You don’t have to feel fearless. I believe in you.”"},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-014","family_key":"comfort_and_reassurance","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"self_doubt_needs_specific_reassurance","scenario":"They are second-guessing their effort or ability and would benefit from specific reassurance.","required_evidence":"Direct self-doubt plus evidence of effort or an invitation for reassurance.","disqualifiers":"Empty praise; grand promises; treating insecurity as a permanent trait.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"gentle","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"A LITTLE REASSURANCE, REMIND THEM","template_card":{"label":"A LITTLE REASSURANCE","title":"They’re Forgetting Their Own Evidence","observation":"They are second-guessing themselves while overlooking the effort and follow-through already behind them.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Name one specific thing you have seen them handle well."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-015","family_key":"comfort_and_reassurance","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"overwhelmed_needs_emotional_safety","scenario":"They feel overwhelmed and want permission not to have everything together.","required_evidence":"Explicit overload plus shame, pressure to appear okay, or desire for emotional safety.","disqualifiers":"Generic busyness; assuming crisis; taking over without consent.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"gentle","depth_level":"L5 Full","field_pattern":"Observation, distinct meaning, and one proportionate takeaway. Use only when each adds value.","label_options":"SAFE TO UNRAVEL, NO PERFORMANCE","template_card":{"label":"NO PERFORMANCE","title":"They Don’t Need to Hold It Together Here","observation":"They are tired of presenting a composed version of themselves while carrying more than they can comfortably manage.","meaning":"A small response fits better here than trying to solve the whole situation.","takeaway":"Tell them: “You don’t have to make it sound okay with me.”"},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-016","family_key":"comfort_and_reassurance","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"feeling_left_out","scenario":"They feel excluded and want their hurt recognized.","required_evidence":"Direct statement of feeling left out plus openness to care or connection.","disqualifiers":"Assuming deliberate exclusion; escalating conflict; blaming named people.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"gentle","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"FEELING OUTSIDE, A LITTLE CARE","template_card":{"label":"FEELING OUTSIDE","title":null,"observation":"They are sitting with the sting of being left out, even while recognizing that nobody may have meant to hurt them.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Acknowledge the hurt before trying to explain anyone else’s intentions."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-017","family_key":"comfort_and_reassurance","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"rough_day_wants_affection","scenario":"They directly express wanting affection, tenderness, or extra love after a hard day.","required_evidence":"Explicit desire for affection, a hug, closeness, or gentle care.","disqualifiers":"Assuming physical affection; relationship type where romantic language is inappropriate.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"gentle","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"EXTRA LOVE, SOFT LANDING","template_card":{"label":"SOFT LANDING","title":"Words Can Be Optional","observation":"They are craving comfort that feels simple and safe rather than another conversation they have to carry.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Offer the closest version of a hug your relationship and distance allow."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-018","family_key":"comfort_and_reassurance","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"missing_viewer_explicitly","scenario":"They explicitly miss the viewer and want closeness.","required_evidence":"Direct statement that they miss the viewer or a shared routine.","disqualifiers":"Inferring longing from nostalgia; using guilt; demanding immediate contact.","emotional_weight":"ordinary","tone_mode":"gentle_practical","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"MISSING YOU, CLOSE THE GAP","template_card":{"label":"CLOSE THE GAP","title":"They Miss the Unremarkable Parts Too","observation":"They are missing the easy, ordinary presence between you more than any big occasion.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Share one small piece of your current day instead of sending a formal update."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-019","family_key":"comfort_and_reassurance","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"ashamed_after_mistake","scenario":"They feel ashamed after a mistake and need care without erasing accountability.","required_evidence":"Direct shame or self-criticism plus acknowledged mistake.","disqualifiers":"Excusing harm; declaring the mistake harmless; instructing the viewer to forgive.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"restrained","depth_level":"L5 Full","field_pattern":"Observation, distinct meaning, and one proportionate takeaway. Use only when each adds value.","label_options":"CARE WITHOUT ERASING, HUMAN MOMENT","template_card":{"label":"HUMAN MOMENT","title":"A Mistake Is Taking Up the Whole Mirror","observation":"They are taking responsibility, but their self-judgment has grown larger than the specific thing they did.","meaning":"A small response fits better here than trying to solve the whole situation.","takeaway":"Separate the person from the mistake while respecting the repair still needed."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-020","family_key":"comfort_and_reassurance","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"anniversary_or_memory_day","scenario":"A personally difficult date or memory is weighing on them and they welcome gentle acknowledgment.","required_evidence":"Explicit mention of the date or memory and openness to acknowledgment.","disqualifiers":"Guessing anniversaries; naming private loss details; forcing remembrance.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"restrained","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"GENTLE DAY, HOLD IT LIGHTLY","template_card":{"label":"GENTLE DAY","title":"A Small Acknowledgment Is Enough","observation":"A difficult memory is close to the surface, and they want it recognized without having to carry a large conversation.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Send a brief note that remembers the day and leaves the door open."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-021","family_key":"space_and_boundaries","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"social_battery_empty","scenario":"Their social energy is depleted and they explicitly want less interaction.","required_evidence":"Direct low-social-energy language plus a preference for quiet, delay, or no reply.","disqualifiers":"Silence alone; assuming rejection; disappearing without any sign of care.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"gentle","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"LOW BATTERY, QUIET MODE","template_card":{"label":"LOW BATTERY","title":"Not Ignoring You. Just Full.","observation":"Their days have left very little social energy available, and replying may feel like one more demand right now.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Send one no-reply-needed check-in, then let the conversation rest."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-022","family_key":"space_and_boundaries","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"overstimulated_needs_quiet","scenario":"They are overstimulated and want fewer inputs for a while.","required_evidence":"Explicit overwhelm from noise, people, screens, or demands plus stated need for quiet.","disqualifiers":"Diagnosing sensory conditions; one annoyance; adding a call without permission.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"restrained","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"LESS INPUT, NEEDS QUIET","template_card":{"label":"LESS INPUT","title":"Quiet Is the Helpful Thing","observation":"They have reached the point where even well-meant interaction could feel like more input to process.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Keep contact brief and let them choose when to reopen the door."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-023","family_key":"space_and_boundaries","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"after_conflict_needs_cooldown","scenario":"They explicitly need time to cool down before discussing a conflict.","required_evidence":"Direct request for time or statement that they are too activated to talk productively.","disqualifiers":"Using space as indefinite avoidance; urgent safety issue; pressuring for immediate resolution.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"restrained","depth_level":"L5 Full","field_pattern":"Observation, distinct meaning, and one proportionate takeaway. Use only when each adds value.","label_options":"COOL-DOWN TIME, PAUSE FIRST","template_card":{"label":"PAUSE FIRST","title":"Space Can Protect the Conversation","observation":"They know they are not ready to speak in a way that reflects what they actually want to say.","meaning":"A small response fits better here than trying to solve the whole situation.","takeaway":"Acknowledge the pause and agree on a gentle time to check back."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-024","family_key":"space_and_boundaries","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"deadline_focus_no_interruptions","scenario":"They need uninterrupted focus during a short, high-demand period.","required_evidence":"A defined deadline plus explicit request for fewer interruptions or delayed contact.","disqualifiers":"Generic busyness; turning temporary focus into emotional distance; detailed confidential schedule.","emotional_weight":"ordinary","tone_mode":"gentle_practical","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"HEAD-DOWN MODE, FOCUS WINDOW","template_card":{"label":"FOCUS WINDOW","title":"They’re Protecting Their Attention","observation":"They are temporarily narrowing their world around a deadline and have clarified that reduced contact is about focus.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Send support once, then wait until the focus window has passed."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-025","family_key":"space_and_boundaries","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"alone_time_to_reset","scenario":"They explicitly use alone time to recover and want it respected.","required_evidence":"Direct preference for solitude plus stated restorative function.","disqualifiers":"Loneliness; punitive silence; assuming all future contact is unwelcome.","emotional_weight":"ordinary","tone_mode":"gentle_practical","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"RESET SOLO, ALONE ON PURPOSE","template_card":{"label":"ALONE ON PURPOSE","title":"Solitude Is Doing Useful Work","observation":"They are choosing time alone as a way to recover, not as a signal that they care less.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Let the evening stay theirs and reconnect after they have had room to land."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-026","family_key":"space_and_boundaries","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"no_reply_needed_preference","scenario":"They want care that does not create an obligation to respond.","required_evidence":"Explicit preference for no-reply-needed messages or difficulty keeping up with responses.","disqualifiers":"No evidence of preference; repeated messages; using the phrase manipulatively.","emotional_weight":"ordinary","tone_mode":"gentle_practical","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"QUIET CARE, NO REPLY NEEDED","template_card":{"label":"QUIET CARE","title":null,"observation":"They appreciate being remembered, but the expectation to answer can turn comfort into another obligation.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Try: “Thinking of you. No need to reply.”"},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-027","family_key":"space_and_boundaries","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"decision_needs_private_thinking","scenario":"They want to think through a personal decision privately before discussing it.","required_evidence":"Direct boundary around when or whether they want to discuss the decision.","disqualifiers":"Medical, legal, or financial specifics; pressing for access; interpreting privacy as distrust.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"restrained","depth_level":"L5 Full","field_pattern":"Observation, distinct meaning, and one proportionate takeaway. Use only when each adds value.","label_options":"THEIR PROCESS, THINKING SPACE","template_card":{"label":"THEIR PROCESS","title":"They Want Their Own Voice First","observation":"They are protecting enough quiet to understand what they think before other opinions enter the room.","meaning":"A small response fits better here than trying to solve the whole situation.","takeaway":"Respect the pause and let them be the one to bring the decision back."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-028","family_key":"space_and_boundaries","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"family_stress_no_questions","scenario":"They are dealing with family stress and explicitly do not want questions yet.","required_evidence":"Direct mention of family stress plus a boundary against details or questions.","disqualifiers":"Requesting private family details; assuming conflict roles; disappearing entirely.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"restrained","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"CARE QUIETLY, NO QUESTIONS YET","template_card":{"label":"CARE QUIETLY","title":"Support Without the Debrief","observation":"They want to feel accompanied without turning private family stress into something they have to explain.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Send warmth without questions and let them decide if details ever come later."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-029","family_key":"space_and_boundaries","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"quiet_evening_boundary","scenario":"They have clearly reserved an evening for low-demand recovery.","required_evidence":"Explicit plan for quiet plus stated need or benefit.","disqualifiers":"One routine night at home; assuming all contact is unwelcome.","emotional_weight":"ordinary","tone_mode":"gentle_practical","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"OFF-DUTY, LET THEM LAND","template_card":{"label":"OFF-DUTY","title":"Tonight Has a Very Small Agenda","observation":"They have deliberately made the evening low-demand because even simple decisions feel like extra weight.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Avoid adding plans or questions; a single warm reaction is enough."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-030","family_key":"space_and_boundaries","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"boundary_around_specific_topic","scenario":"They are open to connection but do not want one particular topic discussed.","required_evidence":"A clear topic boundary plus evidence that other forms of contact remain welcome.","disqualifiers":"Hidden topic; probing around the boundary; treating it as permanent.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"restrained","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"TOPIC OFFLINE, OTHER DOORS OPEN","template_card":{"label":"OTHER DOORS OPEN","title":"Connection Is Welcome. That Topic Isn’t.","observation":"They still want contact, but one part of life has already taken enough of their attention.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Reach out with something unrelated and leave the blocked topic alone."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-031","family_key":"encouragement","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"before_important_presentation","scenario":"They want a brief confidence boost before an important presentation.","required_evidence":"Upcoming presentation plus explicit nerves and openness to encouragement.","disqualifiers":"Advice request not present; exact confidential schedule; inflated promises.","emotional_weight":"ordinary","tone_mode":"gentle_practical","depth_level":"L5 Full","field_pattern":"Observation, distinct meaning, and one proportionate takeaway. Use only when each adds value.","label_options":"LITTLE BOOST, BIG MOMENT","template_card":{"label":"LITTLE BOOST","title":"Cheerleader Duty, Activated","observation":"They have finished preparing and are no longer looking for another round of fixes. Confidence is the useful contribution now.","meaning":"A small response fits better here than trying to solve the whole situation.","takeaway":"Send: “You’ve put in the work. Go show them what you built.”"},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-032","family_key":"encouragement","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"before_exam","scenario":"They want calm encouragement before a meaningful exam.","required_evidence":"Upcoming exam plus preparation and a stated or clearly grounded desire for encouragement.","disqualifiers":"Pressure about scores; claiming guaranteed success; study advice not requested.","emotional_weight":"ordinary","tone_mode":"gentle_practical","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"YOU’VE GOT THIS, STEADY BOOST","template_card":{"label":"STEADY BOOST","title":"Trust the Work Already Done","observation":"They have prepared seriously, but nerves are making that effort harder for them to feel.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Remind them that the goal is to show up, not to feel perfectly calm."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-033","family_key":"encouragement","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"before_job_interview","scenario":"They need grounded confidence before an interview or opportunity.","required_evidence":"Confirmed opportunity plus nerves, self-doubt, or explicit desire for support.","disqualifiers":"Career prediction; salary details; unsolicited coaching.","emotional_weight":"ordinary","tone_mode":"gentle_practical","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"NEXT-STEP ENERGY, LITTLE HYPE","template_card":{"label":"NEXT-STEP ENERGY","title":"Their Nerves Are Editing the Résumé","observation":"They care about the opportunity, and anxiety is making them discount the experience that earned the interview.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Name one real strength they bring instead of promising the outcome."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-034","family_key":"encouragement","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"sharing_creative_work","scenario":"They are nervous about sharing creative work and want supportive attention.","required_evidence":"Upcoming or recent share plus vulnerability and openness to encouragement.","disqualifiers":"Unrequested critique; exaggerated praise; public sharing without consent.","emotional_weight":"ordinary","tone_mode":"gentle_practical","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"BRAVE SHARE, CREATIVE COURAGE","template_card":{"label":"BRAVE SHARE","title":"Being Seen Is the Hard Part","observation":"The vulnerable step is not finishing the work; it is letting other people see something personal.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Celebrate the courage to share before commenting on the result."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-035","family_key":"encouragement","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"first_day_new_role","scenario":"They are entering a new role and need reassurance about being new.","required_evidence":"Confirmed first day or early transition plus nerves and openness to support.","disqualifiers":"Assuming incompetence; giving a long list of advice; exact workplace details.","emotional_weight":"ordinary","tone_mode":"gentle_practical","depth_level":"L5 Full","field_pattern":"Observation, distinct meaning, and one proportionate takeaway. Use only when each adds value.","label_options":"FIRST-DAY ENERGY, NEW CHAPTER","template_card":{"label":"FIRST-DAY ENERGY","title":"New Doesn’t Mean Unready","observation":"They are comparing their first day with other people’s accumulated experience.","meaning":"A small response fits better here than trying to solve the whole situation.","takeaway":"Try: “You’re allowed to be new. You still belong in the room.”"},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-036","family_key":"encouragement","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"habit_progress_needs_recognition","scenario":"They are making steady progress and want it noticed before the final result.","required_evidence":"Repeated effort plus direct pride, discouragement, or desire for recognition.","disqualifiers":"Body judgment; productivity pressure; generic applause with no evidence.","emotional_weight":"ordinary","tone_mode":"gentle_practical","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"PROGRESS COUNTS, KEEP GOING","template_card":{"label":"PROGRESS COUNTS","title":null,"observation":"They have built real consistency, even though the unfinished goal is making that progress easy to overlook.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Recognize the pattern they have sustained, not only the finish line."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-037","family_key":"encouragement","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"setback_during_comeback","scenario":"A setback is shaking confidence during an otherwise meaningful return.","required_evidence":"Evidence of prior progress, a recent setback, and discouragement.","disqualifiers":"Medical or injury details; minimizing the setback; demanding immediate return.","emotional_weight":"sensitive","tone_mode":"gentle","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"ONE ROUGH ROUND, COMEBACK CONTINUES","template_card":{"label":"ONE ROUGH ROUND","title":"Today Doesn’t Erase the Comeback","observation":"One difficult attempt is making a longer stretch of progress feel smaller than it is.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Remind them of one concrete way they have already moved forward."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-038","family_key":"encouragement","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"applying_for_opportunity","scenario":"They are hesitating to pursue an opportunity because of self-doubt.","required_evidence":"A concrete opportunity plus desire to apply and fear holding them back.","disqualifiers":"Pressuring them to apply; claiming they will get it; private employer details.","emotional_weight":"ordinary","tone_mode":"gentle_practical","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"GO FOR IT, OPEN DOOR","template_card":{"label":"OPEN DOOR","title":"The Doubt Arrived Before the Decision","observation":"They are interested in the opportunity, but self-doubt is trying to close it before anyone else can respond.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Encourage the attempt without attaching their worth to the outcome."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-039","family_key":"encouragement","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"before_performance_or_competition","scenario":"They want encouragement before a performance or competition.","required_evidence":"Confirmed upcoming moment plus preparation and nerves.","disqualifiers":"Guaranteed victory; pressure to perform; detailed itinerary.","emotional_weight":"ordinary","tone_mode":"gentle_practical","depth_level":"L5 Full","field_pattern":"Observation, distinct meaning, and one proportionate takeaway. Use only when each adds value.","label_options":"GAME FACE, MOMENT AHEAD","template_card":{"label":"GAME FACE","title":"The Nerves Know It Matters","observation":"They have prepared for this moment, and the intensity is making confidence come and go.","meaning":"A small response fits better here than trying to solve the whole situation.","takeaway":"Send one grounded reminder of the work they have already done."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-040","family_key":"encouragement","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"quiet_win_needs_celebration","scenario":"They achieved something meaningful but are minimizing it.","required_evidence":"A concrete win plus explicit minimization or uncertainty about celebrating.","disqualifiers":"Inflating a routine task; public celebration without consent; comparing achievements.","emotional_weight":"ordinary","tone_mode":"gentle_practical","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"LET IT COUNT, TINY CELEBRATION","template_card":{"label":"LET IT COUNT","title":"Small Doesn’t Mean Meaningless","observation":"They reached a finish that required real effort, but are already shrinking it because it may look ordinary from the outside.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Mark the win in a way that matches its size but still lets it count."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-041","family_key":"practical_help","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"errands_overload_accepts_help","scenario":"Routine errands are piling up and they are open to concrete help.","required_evidence":"Specific logistical overload plus explicit openness to assistance.","disqualifiers":"Assuming incapacity; taking control; purchases or spending without permission.","emotional_weight":"ordinary","tone_mode":"gentle_practical","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"ONE THING OFF, PRACTICAL CARE","template_card":{"label":"ONE THING OFF","title":"Make the Help Smaller and Real","observation":"They do not need the whole week rescued. One concrete task removed would create meaningful breathing room.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Offer one specific errand you can realistically handle, and let them choose."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-042","family_key":"practical_help","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"meal_support_requested","scenario":"They have little capacity for food preparation and welcome meal support.","required_evidence":"Direct difficulty feeding themselves plus openness to food help.","disqualifiers":"Diet, body, medical, or eating-disorder inference; ordering without permission.","emotional_weight":"ordinary","tone_mode":"gentle_practical","depth_level":"L4 Action","field_pattern":"Observation and one low-pressure takeaway. Meaning is optional.","label_options":"DINNER HELP, EASY CARE","template_card":{"label":"DINNER HELP","title":"One Less Decision at the End of the Day","observation":"By evening, even deciding what to eat has become another task competing for limited energy.","meaning":null,"takeaway":"Offer a simple meal option and ask before arranging anything."},"blocked_overlap":"Do not retell the source event. Keep this card focused on the supported response or opening.","library_version":"v2"},{"template_id":"A-043","family_key":"practical_help","section":"ways_in","module_key":null,"scenario_key":"moving_help_requested","scenario":"They are preparing for a move and directly welcome hands-on help.","required_evidence":"Confirmed move plus a specific invitation or openness to packing, sorting, or practical support.","disqualifiers":"Exact address; assuming access to their home; expensive commitments.","emotional_weight":"ordinary","tone_mode":"gentle_practical","depth_level":"L5 Full","field_pattern":"Observation, distinct meaning, and one proportionate takeaway. Use only when each adds value.","label_options":"EXTRA HANDS, MOVING WEEK","template_card":{"label":"EXTRA HANDS","title":"This Is a Hands-On Kind of Care","observation":"The move